hs but then  we had a month break and during that  month  it seemed that everything he had learned  during the autumn  matured in a way he came back in january  clearly with grandmaster level strength  it became really big when we were in  iceland  uh in 2004 and he played kasparov in  cardboard  gary casparo was ranked number one in  the world minus  somehow tricked him in the opening it is  wed in hell of a town  it was so weird with all the media it  was the first time i think we  experienced that that  the pressure was so high from outside  dad was getting more and more excited  when he played against kasparov and we  were like oh my god is  is she actually not losing i still very  much remember  the the the nervousness that i felt on  the day  on the game where i finally got the  title and my  opponent i think offered a draw in in a  somewhat worse position and  frankly i mean i couldn't have uh  couldn't have taken the draw any faster  we went to celebrate at mcdonald's  which was like not like where we would  go to eat every day and even got  ice cream so proud dad  that's the international grandmaster  title  diploma that he received from fida so at  13 he became one of the  youngest ever  [Music]  it's funny to think of that it's almost  17  years ago i've been now groundmaster for  much longer than i haven't  i have worked with him since 2009.  minus was then 19. what was he like he  was a bit different from now  actually i think it was quite shy it's  difficult to  get him to do things that he wasn't  used to do when he started to get  recognized on the streets more often in  oslo that  that did not go down very well with him  but i think he was really happy that  normal people who would not usually  follow chess  being interested in in it i think that's  what he thought was really great about  it if i were to become world champion  that would be great  magnus carlsen this is his first  world championship match  this was a larger than life experience  you have this  exotic feel the smells  the noise it's so overwhelming  and together with hundreds of  journalists  it was such an uh mesmerizing  experience a team of grandmasters knows  everything about magna skulls  and they're off  i think i said after the match that well  now i can die  we had a nice celebration and it was a  very happy night for everyone involved  when he won in the end  but at that point he he he was already  there mentally in a way i mean  this was his to win it was like a force  [Music]  2018 carano that was a tough one  you had a great year i didn't and it  felt  when we were playing like we were equals  the other matches it's felt like  losing is simply not an option it cannot  happen obviously that's  not an attitude that is good if you want  to have  an enjoyable experience the match in  london was an equal match and  if i'd lost it would have hurt a great  deal but  still it didn't feel like it was  impossible  you can just feel it when your intuition  doesn't work  it's just the feeling of something's  gone horribly horribly wrong  i think that's something of the most  stressful that can be in sports to  sit there three weeks against the same  opponent and  needing to have a good sleep every night  and it's so stressful  so much nerves i'm not at all able to  understand how he's  able to play under that pressure and  those conditions at all because  it's inhumane after i gained the title  i didn't want to lose it i'm not  necessarily that happy that i have it i  just would be very  unhappy to not have it then the first  you have something to achieve that you  haven't achieved before  after that you either repeat or  fall back down and psychologically  that's much more difficult  for how long do you see yourself  motivated now to keep  defend your title i will most probably  play in  2021 and if i were to win  i have no idea whether i would play the  next one  [Music]  [Music]  foreign

